    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "546:281",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Fire Station",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Fire Station"
        },
        {
          "text": "A Tour of the Fire Station\n\nOur school organised a trip to the local fire station last week. The firefighters were friendly and showed us everything.\n\nThe station has a large garage where the fire engines are parked. Each truck carries hoses, ladders, axes, and first aid equipment. The firefighters explained that a fire engine can carry over a thousand litres of water in its tank.\n\nWe saw the firefighters' uniforms hanging in a row near the garage: helmets, fireproof jackets, heavy boots, and breathing apparatus. They told us they can get dressed in under sixty seconds when the alarm goes off.\n\nUpstairs, there is a common room where the crew rests between calls. It has a kitchen, a dining table, and some sofas. Next to it, there is a dormitory with bunk beds for night shifts. When the alarm sounds, the firefighters slide down a pole to reach the garage quickly.\n\nThe station also has a training tower where firefighters practise climbing ladders and rescuing people from height. Outside, there is a yard with a practice area for using hoses and extinguishers.\n\nThe fire chief gave us a talk about fire safety. She explained the importance of smoke alarms, fire exits, and escape plans. She showed us how to use a fire extinguisher: Pull the pin, Aim at the base, Squeeze the handle, and Sweep side to side — the PASS technique.\n\nAt the end of the visit, we got to sit in a fire engine and turn on the siren. It was an exciting and educational day.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "A Tour of the Fire Station Our school organised a trip to the local fire station last week. The firefighters were friendly and showed us everything. The station has a large garage where the fire engines are parked. Each truck carries hoses, ladders, axes, and first aid equipment. The firefighters explained that a fire engine can carry over a thousand litres of water in its tank. We saw the firefighters' uniforms hanging in a row near the garage: helmets, fireproof jackets, heavy boots, and breathing apparatus. They told us they can get dressed in under sixty seconds when the alarm goes off. Upstairs, there is a common room where the crew rests between calls. It has a kitchen, a dining table, and some sofas. Next to it, there is a dormitory with bunk beds for night shifts. When the alarm sounds, the firefighters slide down a pole to reach the garage quickly. The station also has a training tower where firefighters practise climbing ladders and rescuing people from height. Outside, there is a yard with a practice area for using hoses and extinguishers. The fire chief gave us a talk about fire safety. She explained the importance of smoke alarms, fire exits, and escape plans. She showed us how to use a fire extinguisher: Pull the pin, Aim at the base, Squeeze the handle, and Sweep side to side — the PASS technique. At the end of the visit, we got to sit in a fire engine and turn on the siren. It was an exciting and educational day."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. What equipment does a fire engine carry?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. What equipment does a fire engine carry?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. How quickly can firefighters get dressed?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. How quickly can firefighters get dressed?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What is the training tower used for?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What is the training tower used for?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. What does PASS stand for?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. What does PASS stand for?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. What did the fire chief talk about?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. What did the fire chief talk about?"
        }
      ]
    },
    "idioms-phrases": {
      "nodeId": "546:294",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases"
        },
        {
          "text": "fight fire with fire",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "fight fire with fire"
        },
        {
          "text": "respond to an attack using the same methods",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "respond to an attack using the same methods"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Sometimes you have to fight fire with fire.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"Sometimes you have to fight fire with fire.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "put out",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "put out"
        },
        {
          "text": "extinguish a fire",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "extinguish a fire"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The firefighters put out the blaze in thirty minutes.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"The firefighters put out the blaze in thirty minutes.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "spread like wildfire",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "spread like wildfire"
        },
        {
          "text": "spread very quickly",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "spread very quickly"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The news spread like wildfire through the neighbourhood.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"The news spread like wildfire through the neighbourhood.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "under fire",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "under fire"
        },
        {
          "text": "being attacked or criticised",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "being attacked or criticised"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The company came under fire for the safety failure.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"The company came under fire for the safety failure.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "set off",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "set off"
        },
        {
          "text": "activate (an alarm); also: begin a journey",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "activate (an alarm); also: begin a journey"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The smoke set off the fire alarm in the hallway.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"The smoke set off the fire alarm in the hallway.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "break out",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "break out"
        },
        {
          "text": "start suddenly (fire, war, disease)",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "start suddenly (fire, war, disease)"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"A fire broke out on the third floor of the building.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"A fire broke out on the third floor of the building.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "call out",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "call out"
        },
        {
          "text": "summon for help; also: criticise publicly",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "summon for help; also: criticise publicly"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The fire brigade was called out three times last night.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"The fire brigade was called out three times last night.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "smoke and mirrors",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "smoke and mirrors"
        },
        {
          "text": "something designed to deceive or confuse",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "something designed to deceive or confuse"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The politician's answer was all smoke and mirrors.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"The politician's answer was all smoke and mirrors.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "where there's smoke, there's fire",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "where there's smoke, there's fire"
        },
        {
          "text": "if there are signs of a problem, the problem probably exists",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "if there are signs of a problem, the problem probably exists"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"He denied it, but where there's smoke, there's fire.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"He denied it, but where there's smoke, there's fire.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "get out / evacuate",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "get out / evacuate"
        },
        {
          "text": "leave a building quickly in an emergency",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "leave a building quickly in an emergency"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Get out of the building immediately — the alarm is real!\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"Get out of the building immediately — the alarm is real!\""
        }
      ]
    },
    "mini-dialogue": {
      "nodeId": "546:338",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "🗣️ Mini Dialogue",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "🗣️ Mini Dialogue"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scene: A firefighter teaching children about fire safety",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Scene: A firefighter teaching children about fire safety"
        },
        {
          "text": "Firefighter:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Firefighter:"
        },
        {
          "text": "Does anyone know what you should do if you smell smoke at home?",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Does anyone know what you should do if you smell smoke at home?"
        },
        {
          "text": "Student:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Student:"
        },
        {
          "text": "Get out of the house?",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Get out of the house?"
        },
        {
          "text": "Firefighter:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Firefighter:"
        },
        {
          "text": "Exactly. Get out, stay out, and call 999. Never go back inside.",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Exactly. Get out, stay out, and call 999. Never go back inside."
        },
        {
          "text": "Student:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Student:"
        },
        {
          "text": "What if the door is hot?",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "What if the door is hot?"
        },
        {
          "text": "Firefighter:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Firefighter:"
        },
        {
          "text": "Good question. Feel the door with the back of your hand. If it's hot, don't open it.",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Good question. Feel the door with the back of your hand. If it's hot, don't open it."
        },
        {
          "text": "Student:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Student:"
        },
        {
          "text": "What about smoke alarms? We have one in the kitchen.",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "What about smoke alarms? We have one in the kitchen."
        },
        {
          "text": "Firefighter:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Firefighter:"
        },
        {
          "text": "Every home should have one on each floor. Test them once a month.",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Every home should have one on each floor. Test them once a month."
        },
        {
          "text": "Student:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Student:"
        },
        {
          "text": "Can we try using a fire extinguisher?",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Can we try using a fire extinguisher?"
        },
        {
          "text": "Firefighter:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Firefighter:"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not today, but remember PASS: Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep.",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Not today, but remember PASS: Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep."
        },
        {
          "text": "Student:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Student:"
        },
        {
          "text": "How fast can a fire engine go?",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "How fast can a fire engine go?"
        },
        {
          "text": "Firefighter:",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "Firefighter:"
        },
        {
          "text": "Very fast! But safety always comes first — even for us.",
